  "body": "## Status: research note / scoped recursive-interface construction; no new kappa\n\nLinear reader-defect repair does not account for a quadratic dirty reader's mixed term. This package preserves fixed `y += beta_i*a^2; a += alpha_i*b` calls, then fuses the paid correction frame with source restoration. The seed-selected eight-call pilot costs **32 -> 31 exact scalar operations**, including all nonunit multiplications; its square-only correction costs 35. A written determinant argument proves the minimum appended square-query count is two when the mixed defect is nonzero, in the explicitly restricted additive-repair/linear-frame class.\n\nThis is a nonlinear successor to Adam Gall's #1205 and Hanson Sun's #1246, whose notes and attribution are retained unchanged. The contribution adds the quadratic defect, one-product restoring repair, restricted square-call floor, and complete nonlinear tariff. It does not claim the earlier linear mechanisms or a new supplier. If the toy calls can be opened, one direct square and scaling is cheaper; fixed calls are essential.\n\nOnly `research/quadratic-reader-restoration/` is added. Its README gives the proof, full arithmetic/access/child/storage accounting, implemented recursion and next question. The exact child-price gate is `P+3C < (r-2)L`; an expensive product backend can erase the saving. No fixed-tape, scratch-backend, rounding or hosting realization is established. The selected frontier, upstream inputs and frozen packages are unchanged.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/quadratic-reader-restoration\n```\n\nExpected final marker: `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/quadratic-reader-restoration outcome=completed`.\n\nPassing local evidence:\n\n- All 1,364 signed batches of lengths 1-5, full rational polynomial coefficients, 36,828 dirty numeric triples, both repair alphabets and literal inverses.\n- Arity 2-16 exact costs and an independent addressed-read/write observer; binary recursion depths 0-3, complete endpoint/restoration/inverse and invoice checks.\n- Eight semantic/resource controls, including a `4ab` defect invisible on every coordinate basis input and an extra read that preserves the output but fails the bill.\n- Optimized Python 3.12.13 registered replay, source-export relocation and five on-disk corruption rejections; normal Python 3.14.5 independent replay. Source binding, metadata pins and whitespace checks pass.\n\nBase: `ef5f39403610d231a0c27e8a6b4f08c10209bcd6`; OS assignment seed **55**, recursive interfaces. Selected context is reviewed PR1094, `kappa=836330098538459/500000000000000000`. Source pins: PR1205 `e2008d7ffcad464da7ec21c69e8d8a8c91de4930`; PR1246 `5ed1ce17a9df4c853a93f9758ba903d2620c3443`; both heads rechecked unchanged. Git blobs and SHA256 pins are provided. No full selected cold replay, native admission, formal multiplication proof or hosted CI success is claimed.\n\nNo pinned coordination issue existed, so the claim is local. Full open-PR/Discussion overlap metadata was refreshed before submission. The closest linear repair is credited explicitly; broader quadratic/restoration hits concern phase, precision or decoder objects. Search coverage and its limits are recorded, without a novelty guarantee.\n\nPrepared by **Sricharan Vagvala (@theon199)** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance** in algebra, implementation, verification and writing. Apache-2.0. This is exact implementation evidence and a written scoped bound, not independent human review.\n",
